    "chunk_text": "17A IV(\u0d85) \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3 - \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba - 2019.12.05 PART IV(A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 05.12.2019\n\nRATHNAPURA PRADESHIYA SABHA\n\nBy- Law Regarding Food Supply Places\n\nBy-Law on the Maintenance of Food Supply Places in the Rathnapura Pradeshiya Sabha Authoritative Area\n\n1. This By-Law is enacted to regulate, administrate and control the supply of food places within the Authoritative Area of the Rathnapura Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\n2. This By-Law is known as the By-Law for the maintenance of food supply places within the Authoritative Area of the Rathnapura Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\n3. (1) Any person without a valid license issued by the Chairman should not run a food supply place of any premises within the Rathnapura Pradeshiya Sabha Authoritative Area (hereinafter referred to as Authoritative area).\n\n3. (2) A person who wishes to obtain a license in accordance with section 3(1) above shall apply by an application prepared in accordance with the first schedule of this By-Law.\n\n3. (3) The fee for a license under this section shall be the fee determined by the Sabha in accordance with the provisions of the Basic Law.\n\n4. (1) Any person who wishes to commence and maintain a premises subject to a permit under section 3 of this By-Law shall have his prior approval under this By-Law, unless the applicant is entitled to such license, there is no entitlement to apply for a license under section 10 of the by \u2013law.\n\n4. (2) The Chairman shall approve the report of the Public Health Inspector and the Medical Officer of Health on a request for prior approval under this section.\n\n4. (3) The inspection fee to be charged under the approval of this section may be determined by the Sabha from time to time by the resolutions for the purpose.\n\n5. Every person applying for a license under section 3 of this By-Law must meet the following conditions:\n\n5. (1) Approval under section 4 of this By-Law when a business is a start-up business."
